# An Educational Theory Based on Game Theory. Preliminary Work.

**Authors:** Chapman, Laura Hill

## Abstract
Game theory may be a fruitful basis for educational theory. After describing games and related concepts like "utility," the author sets up examples of how games may be used as a basis for selecting teaching strategies. For instance, a teacher may decide to change many aspects of his teaching style, rather than just one at a time, if there is a greater probability that the changes will affect his pupil's performance. (JK)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=ED059621

